Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:53:52 +0800
Subject: [09/14] docs: rewrite README section 8 for v1.6; document estimator
 robustness

README section 8 now covers the six identified problems (R1-R6), what the v1.6
protocol reaches (temperature +0.9 K, energy 1.8e-7, flux symmetry 1.5e-5,
time convergence 12.6 %), the three-way estimator comparison (window 5.3e-9 vs
global fit 1.38e-8 vs plane 1.36e-8), the 0.01 % linear-response check, and the
finding that no pattern beats the flat reference.

STATUS gains a robustness check of the plane estimator: +-7.5 % across the chosen
planes (monotone in Z, so the absolute value must quote Z) but the relative
comparison at fixed Z is unaffected; burn-in 0->50 % raises TBR by 13 %,
confirming the slow drift is real.
